# /etc/hostname
#
# The installer overwrites this. It exists in the base package so that an
# unconfigured image still has a valid, non-empty hostname: systemd refuses to
# start network units with an empty hostname, and a machine reporting an empty
# name to a DHCP server gets no lease.

localhost.localdomain

# A hostname has to be a valid DNS label: letters, digits and hyphens, not
# starting or ending with a hyphen, 63 characters or fewer. Anything else
# breaks DHCP, mDNS and the local resolver in ways that are hard to diagnose.
# The installer validates this and refuses to write an invalid value.